			"Message": "docs(Common): Expand README with service table, directory detail, and engineering principles\n\nOverhaul the Common crate README across several content and formatting dimensions:\n\n- **Badge layout** — Consolidate Rust/Crates.io/Version badges onto single lines with em-quad spacing; add `title=\"Star\"` attribute to the star badge image for accessibility\n- **Overview section** — Remove redundant puzzle emoji from the lead sentence; add a concise four-point \"Common is engineered to\" bullet list covering pure abstractions, compile-time DI, stable data contracts, and transport-agnostic communication\n- **Architecture principles** — Simplify table headers from \"Key Components Involved\" to \"Key Components\" for scannability\n- **Directory tree** — Add `DTO/` subdirectory listings for Configuration, FileSystem, IPC, LanguageFeature, SourceControlManagement, StatusBar, TreeView, UserInterface, and Webview services; add Transport/Common and Transport/Registry; restructure Documentation/ and TypeScript/ directories; include TypeScript runtime source files (Container.ts, EffectSmol.ts, Errors.ts, PubSub.ts, Ref.ts, Result.ts)\n- **Consumer table** — Expand from 3 entries to 6 (adding Grove, Cocoon, Echo); add consistent emoji identifiers and rename section from \"Dependency flow\" to \"Connection paths\"\n- **Getting Started** — Add em-quad heading, Prerequisites subsection, Build subsection, and a new Key Dependencies table (serde, tokio, async-trait, thiserror, posthog-rs, uuid, prometheus)\n- **Compatibility table** — Add emoji identifiers to all integration targets for visual consistency\n- **Related Documentation** — Switch sentence separators from em dash to full em dash (—) throughout\n- **Funding section** — Remove the duplicated NLnet paragraph that repeated the same funding attribution already present",
